### Semantic Memory: Knowledge Base

Semantic memory stores structured knowledge that the agent has accumulated—facts, relationships, and learned concepts. Unlike episodic memory (which stores experiences), semantic memory stores the distilled knowledge extracted from those experiences.

This memory type uses **embeddings** for semantic similarity search, enabling the agent to find relevant knowledge even when queries don't use exact keywords.

