    const { children } = this.props;

    return hasError ? (
      <fallbackComponent />
    ) : (
      children
    );
  }
}

function MyComponent() {
  throw new Error('I crashed!');
}

function App() {
  return (
    <ErrorBoundaryHOC fallbackComponent={<h1>Something went wrong.</h1>}>
      <MyComponent />
    </ErrorBoundaryHOC>
  );
}
```

The Error Boundary HOC implementation is also straightforward and has a minimal impact on performance.

### Custom Error Boundary Class

The custom error boundary class is a more traditional approach that involves creating a class with a lifecycle method to handle errors. Here is an example:

